                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game would be good and entertaining one in it's genre, but it has too many flaws and in fact one that will make last outside area and last boss quite darn hard to beat. First boss you encounter in game is brother of shopkeeper who will sell you such upgrades as triple jump, life extension and gears which give chance to get another upgrade in characters abilities. These abilities would be very much needed in the last boss and later areas in game due double jump will not give you enough boost to reach platforms or hit the boss. \n\nSo basically i have now crying shopkeeper whom with can't interact and get vital upgrades to beat last boss as can't reach and hit him. Wall climbing and getting pair of hits is too slow and there is so much bullethell stuff along with mobs than you will die to those since it takes so long to beat boss that way and mana doesn't recharge fast enough to push through with flaming skull circle spell well and those do vanish with collision of other things than boss.\n\nFlaws seen in the game.\n- Slide tends to be very minor distance and is quite useless, sometimes it does trigger longer distance slide.\n- Double jump tends not to work at some points and game just sucks up the other jump.\n- Wall grip won't happen at some points and for some reason does work on same kind of place in other part of the castle, but then again not in the other.\n- Shortcuts and no teleporting possibilities. Tons of backtracking and those shortcuts often just kill you.\n- Minion and spells reject each other, you can have tiny helper who smacks mobs, but will hit you if you kill his pals and those things are everywhere so you can't use spells beside lightning one as these little things die from anything you do.\n- Some platforming areas suffer from bad decisions like unpassable ridable objects and close zoom because of which you can't see what's before you so basically you will take tons of leap of fates and die trying or get lucky.\n- If you don't lie shopkeeper about death of his brother you will not get vital upgrades.\n- Stunlock, you will get this ton as dmg immunity time is non existent and if you fall on spikes it's miracle if you get out of there before dying due this feature.\n\nI pushed through till the end boss and was annoyed quite much by latest outside area as didn't have needed skill meant for it due game not letting me get it. Did reach overall almost 99% of the map still with double jump skill so it's probably possible to beat the game with only it, but so damn much harder that i'm thinking of first time in long time dropping a game did like. This game has just too many flaws that could recommend it to other people if those would be fixed it would  be quite fun game in it's genre and worthwhile to check out.\n\nIf you decide to get this one, remember to lie to the shopkeeper about the death of his brother so you won't get locked out without skills that will help so much during this game.",
